{"title":"2018 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />), the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69ff720e6d0801983832367327a018e7afce9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=4\\sqrt[3]{abc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"21\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/7043a170ac5535465a5a1b4daccb1f1de3043280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(ab+bc+ca)+4\\min(a^2,b^2,c^2)\\ge a^2+b^2+c^2.\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1df009d16adff7ac78e9a4aabe6315281c3790e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:(0,\\infty) \\rightarrow (0,\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/8945fb40f421318fdb191894bc65db33f0253cd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(x+\\frac{1}{y}\\right)+f\\left(y+\\frac{1}{z}\\right) + f\\left(z+\\frac{1}{x}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"43\" />\nfor all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/2977f3b8dac09821205b23be7a5aabe6e959e5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a2c5e8287e4a17962a54003036fbdd661c8d57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz =1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For a given integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c23df5cef110bc08404e0daa822e20d1cce5ccc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9bec980a937471298078f05068b2c7d3abdcff73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1,a_2,…,a_m\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /> be the set of positive integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Prove that if every prime that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> also divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/0261b7660a32a45170cbb98e39b9129afe0bd916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^k+a_2^k + \\dots + a_m^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />), the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c3130ada36271a164087102045c119516fdfea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\dots, a_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> be integers. Show that there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7624ce20fc9bfb798126ffacdb34110159ef0094.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1 + k, a_2 + 2k, \\dots, a_p + pk\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"17\" />produce at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94a56b75241f2eb79c48ba67c5bc24948152cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2} p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"19\" height=\"21\" /> distinct remainders upon division by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In convex cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/42501e1c7100f340da9bd452bf942219ac6b131b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> we know that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0a1dbdebe8f3df1befc34f5862f69364b3c11b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21c1fa17457c16ebb5ce4d408eb858974fb47143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> and lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e037912024535666d4f5194dcf67a6231061c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> Suppose that the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> intersects line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> intersects line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7d4bc64d1e02c2357e172b4561a714f214138d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,B,P,G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/519cb2162eba6082b872117a4628c27dd5633152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,Q,D,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear in that order. Prove that if lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24ad2dad196a24708c4c056a01a28329e79688d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5142757c2642506afddbe7a80daac9bff8b07766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2eec1d0cc1dbc279797959ade68438faeb160289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MAC = 90^{\\circ}.$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of permutations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7aa0fe15093d0532fabed90b8af5882b8328eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/54085e619c70a42ce4265853b783f64c879ca29a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,\\dots, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> such that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> ratios <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e36ef38bf8ecf58f25252902cace0da979210c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_k}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"21\" height=\"33\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c02d72033414dc27c09c5dd94833f829a9ffcfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le k\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> are all distinct. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is odd for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/4915125d52bc1ed91cd12b4fa842fe363a3915fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO\" title=\"2018 USAMO\">2018 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems\">2017 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems\">2019 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062246\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 315/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 938/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 82/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9785/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.196      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n100.00%    8.196      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16187:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062246 and revision id 205235. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}